Changes (all marked with "Tape In:" comments, found by fuzzing the decoder):
  ALACDecoder.cpp  reject chanBits outside 1..32 (bytesShifted too large for
                   the bit depth would shift by >= 32 in unpc_block)
  ALACDecoder.cpp  reject denShiftU/denShiftV == 0 (unpc_block computes
                   1 << (denshift - 1))
  ALACDecoder.cpp  reject a partial-frame sample count larger than the caller's buffer
                   (it was written to the output and mix buffers unchecked)
  ALACDecoder.cpp  reject mixBits >= 32 (used as a shift count in matrix_dec.c)
  dp_dec.c         unpc_block computed 1 << (denshift - 1) before the numactive == 31
                   branch that the decoder reaches with denshift == 0; now guarded
  The decoder is also compiled with -fwrapv: the predictor's int32 sums
  overflow on malformed input (dp_dec.c:347); wraparound is harmless there.
  ag_dec.c         get_next_fromlong shifted a uint32_t by 32 when the suffix
                   length reached 0 (ag_dec.c:254, found by fuzzing); the macro
                   now returns 0 for a zero-bit suffix. Seed:
                   tests/fuzz/corpus/alac/crash-ag_dec-shift32
